{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"reasoning","text":"Everything matches. Next, I'll write `output/analysis.py`. Write it directly under output/, and execute it with the workspace root as the working directory (using relative paths from the script's location).\n\nKey points of the implementation for pydeseq2 0.5.0:\n- counts_df: samples as rows, genes as columns, integer counts.\n- metadata: index is sample IDs, column is Group (category or str — pydeseq2 requires design factors to be category/str; in 0.5.0 it validates that they're not numeric).\n- DeseqDataSet(counts=counts_df, metadata=metadata, design_factors=\"Group\", ref_level=None, refit_cooks=True)\n- dds.deseq2()\n- DeseqStats(dds, contrast=[\"Group\", \"Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50\", \"DMSO\"]).summary()\n- results_df = stat_res.results_df\n\nPrefiltering: keep genes where max raw count across the 6 samples is > 10.\n\nAlso, note that pydeseq2 might internally require at least some genes, but that's not an issue here.\n\nOne consideration: pydeseq2's DeseqDataSet validates that the counts index matches the metadata index. Also, it might require that the metadata's index order matches. I'll align them.\n\nPotential issue with pandas 3.0: pydeseq2 0.5.0 and pandas 3.0.5 — there might be incompatibilities (e.g., .astype('float') is fine; `DataFrame.append` is removed; `df.applymap` is removed). We'll find out at runtime. If pydeseq2 fails with pandas 3, we might need a venv with an older pandas. Let's try first.\n\nFor null handling in the CSV: pandas' to_csv writes NaN as empty strings by default — this matches \"empty CSV cell\". Good.\n\nFor JSON: json.dump with None.\n\nAlso, record some diagnostic values for the summary: total number of genes in the raw matrix, number of genes after filtering, number with NaN padj, number significant, up/down.\n\nReport: within 500 words, distinguishing statistical association from causation.\n\nAlright, let me write analysis.py. I'll make it deterministic and self-contained, using relative paths based on the script's parent directory (output/), with inputs located at ../inputs.\n\nAlso, sample_layout maps SampleID → Group. In the counts matrix, columns use underscores. I'll derive the counts column by replacing '-' with '_' in the SampleID. I'll load the layout, filter by Group, and select.\n\nEdge case: the layout has 30 rows for 10 groups. Selecting Group == \"Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50\" and \"DMSO\" gives exactly 3 samples each.\n\nNow let me write the script."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"Inputs are fully understood. Now I'll write `output/analysis.py`.\n\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chenyuqiong\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path output | Out-Null; @'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Differential expression analysis: Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50 vs DMSO.\n\nUses PyDESeq2 0.5.0 on the six frozen samples (3 replicates per group) from\ninputs/. Genes are pre-filtered to those with raw count > 10 in at least one\nof the six selected samples. Group is the only design term; the combination\ntreatment is the numerator and DMSO the denominator.\n\nOutputs (written to output/):\n  - differential_expression.csv : full DE table keyed by Ensembl ID\n  - summary.json                : run metadata and counts\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\nimport pydeseq2\nfrom pydeseq2.dds import DeseqDataSet\nfrom pydeseq2.ds import DeseqStats\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent  # workspace root\nINPUTS = ROOT / \\\"inputs\\\"\nOUTDIR = ROOT / \\\"output\\\"\n\nNUMERATOR = \\\"Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50\\\"\nDENOMINATOR = \\\"DMSO\\\"\nPADJ_CUTOFF = 0.05\nLFC_CUTOFF = 0.5\nBASEMEAN_CUTOFF = 10.0\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    # --- Load inputs -------------------------------------------------------\n    layout = pd.read_csv(INPUTS / \\\"sample_layout.csv\\\")\n    counts = pd.read_csv(INPUTS / \\\"counts_raw_unfiltered.csv\\\", index_col=0)\n    gene_map = pd.read_csv(INPUTS / \\\"ensg_to_gene_name.tsv\\\", sep=\\\"\\\\t\\\")\n\n    sel = layout[layout[\\\"Group\\\"].isin([NUMERATOR, DENOMINATOR])].copy()\n    assert sorted(sel[\\\"Group\\\"].value_counts()) == [3, 3], sel\n    sel[\\\"counts_col\\\"] = sel[\\\"SampleID\\\"].str.replace(\\\"-\\\", \\\"_\\\")\n    missing = [c for c in sel[\\\"counts_col\\\"] if c not in counts.columns]\n    assert not missing, missing\n    samples = list(sel[\\\"counts_col\\\"])\n\n    # Six-sample count matrix (samples x genes) and Group metadata.\n    six = counts.loc[:, samples].T\n    six.index.name = \\\"sample\\\"\n    metadata = (\n        sel.set_index(\\\"counts_col\\\")\n        .loc[samples, [\\\"SampleID\\\", \\\"Group\\\"]]\n        .rename_axis(\\\"sample\\\")\n    )\n    assert list(metadata[\\\"Group\\\"].value_counts().sort_index().values) == [3, 3]\n\n    # --- Pre-fit filter: raw count > 10 in at least one of the six samples -\n    keep = six.max(axis=1) > 10\n    six = six.loc[:, keep]\n    six = six.astype(int)\n    n_genes_total = counts.shape[0]\n    n_genes_tested = int(six.shape[1])\n\n    # --- DESeq2 ------------------------------------------------------------\n    dds = DeseqDataSet(\n        counts=six,\n        metadata=metadata,\n        design_factors=\\\"Group\\\",\n        refit_cooks=True,\n    )\n    dds.deseq2()\n    stat_res = DeseqStats(dds, contrast=[\\\"Group\\\", NUMERATOR, DENOMINATOR])\n    stat_res.summary()\n    res = stat_res.results_df.copy()\n    res.index.name = \\\"ensembl_id\\\"\n\n    # --- Passing genes -----------------------------------------------------\n    passed = (\n        (res[\\\"padj\\\"] < PADJ_CUTOFF)\n        & (res[\\\"log2FoldChange\\\"].abs() > LFC_CUTOFF)\n        & (res[\\\"baseMean\\\"] > BASEMEAN_CUTOFF)\n    )\n    passed = passed.fillna(False).astype(bool)\n    res[\\\"passed\\\"] = passed\n\n    res = res.join(\n        gene_map.set_index(\\\"ENSG\\\")[\\\"gene_name\\\"], on=\\\"ensembl_id\\\", how=\\\"left\\\"\n    )\n    cols = [\\\"gene_name\\\", \\\"baseMean\\\", \\\"log2FoldChange\\\", \\\"lfcSE\\\", \\\"stat\\\",\n            \\\"pvalue\\\", \\\"padj\\\", \\\"passed\\\"]\n    res = res[cols]\n\n    csv_path = OUTDIR / \\\"differential_expression.csv\\\"\n    res.to_csv(csv_path)  # NaN -> empty cell (null preserved, never zero)\n\n    # --- Summary -----------------------------------------------------------\n    sig = res.loc[res[\\\"passed\\\"]]\n    summary = {\n        \\\"contrast\\\": f\\\"{NUMERATOR} vs {DENOMINATOR}\\\",\n        \\\"numerator\\\": NUMERATOR,\n        \\\"denominator\\\": DENOMINATOR,\n        \\\"design\\\": \\\"~Group\\\",\n        \\\"samples\\\": {\n            NUMERATOR: sel.loc[sel[\\\"Group\\\"] == NUMERATOR, \\\"SampleID\\\"].tolist(),\n            DENOMINATOR: sel.loc[sel[\\\"Group\\\"] == DENOMINATOR, \\\"SampleID\\\"].tolist(),\n        },\n        \\\"prefilter\\\": \\\"raw count > 10 in at least one of the six selected samples\\\",\n        \\\"n_genes_in_raw_matrix\\\": n_genes_total,\n        \\\"n_genes_tested\\\": n_genes_tested,\n        \\\"n_genes_dropped_by_prefilter\\\": n_genes_total - n_genes_tested,\n        \\\"n_padj_null\\\": int(res[\\\"padj\\\"].isna().sum()),\n        \\\"thresholds\\\": {\n            \\\"padj\\\": PADJ_CUTOFF,\n            \\\"abs_log2FoldChange\\\": LFC_CUTOFF,\n            \\\"baseMean\\\": BASEMEAN_CUTOFF,\n        },\n        \\\"n_passed\\\": int(passed.sum()),\n        \\\"n_up\\\": int((passed & (res[\\\"log2FoldChange\\\"] > 0)).sum()),\n        \\\"n_down\\\": int((passed & (res[\\\"log2FoldChange\\\"] < 0)).sum()),\n        \\\"software\\\": {\n            \\\"pydeseq2\\\": pydeseq2.__version__,\n            \\\"pandas\\\": pd.__version__,\n            \\\"refit_cooks\\\": True,\n        },\n    }\n    with open(OUTDIR / \\\"summary.json\\\", \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\n        json.dump(summary, fh, indent=2)\n\n    print(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n    print(\\\"top passing genes by padj:\\\")\n    print(sig.sort_values(\\\"padj\\\").head(10).to_string())\n\n\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\n    main()\n'@ | Set-Content -Encoding utf8 output/analysis.py; Write-Host 'written'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
